 ### Binary Tree Indexing
-#### definition
-- [S3] A simple binary tree indexing scheme to identify and organize patches in a breadth-first manner (coarse to fine). Allows quick identification of cousin patches [S3]. View-dependent mesh generation uses recursive traversal over the patch hierarchy by indexing into a fixed-size 1D array of patches, accumulating patch IDs for later decompression and rendering [S3].
